      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 77253,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Microprocessor Operations Architecture Hierarchy",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "sub-mu42d03x-15"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-13-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1152,
      "y": -186,
      "width": 306,
      "height": 171,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 411707,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 778663,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The 8085 coordinates all bus activity\nusing control and status signals: IO/M'\ndesignates whether the current cycle\ntargets memory (0) or peripheral I/O\n(1). RD' coordinates read transfers and\nWR' coordinates write transfers.\nTogether, these signals generate MEMR',\nMEMW', IOR', and IOW' strobes via\nexternal gating logic.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-15-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1230,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 152,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 126279,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 44682,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The internal architecture executes\nregister-to-register transfers, ALU\narithmetic (+, -), logical bit\nmanipulation (AND, OR, XOR), flag\ncondition updates, and instruction\ndecoding (IR to ID). External operations\ninterface directly with memory arrays\nand peripheral controllers.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
