    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-10_text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 461,
      "width": 264,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 607242,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 797399,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Bus Write Communication Cycle",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow-mu42d03x-10"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-6-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -651,
      "y": 446,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 190,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 633895,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 673819,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Every computer program reduces to\nfour basic external bus cycles:\nMemory Read (IO/M'=0, RD'=0, WR'=1)\nto fetch opcodes and operands;\nMemory Write (IO/M'=0, RD'=1,\nWR'=0) to store results; I/O Read\n(IO/M'=1, RD'=0, WR'=1) to accept\ndata from sensors/ports; and I/O\nWrite (IO/M'=1, RD'=1, WR'=0) to\noutput data to actuators/displays.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-8-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -485,
      "y": 673,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 114,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 749409,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 842372,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The microprocessor places a 16-bit\naddress on the address bus to select the\ntargeted memory location or I/O port via\naddress decoders, asserts the active-low\nRD' strobe, and latches data driven onto\nD7-D0 into internal registers.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-10-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 538,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 95,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 185452,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 502253,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The CPU asserts the targeted 16-bit\naddress, drives computed data onto data\nbus lines D7-D0, and emits an active-low\nWR' strobe pulse to latch the data byte\npermanently into the external device.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "diagram-mu42d03x-12",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 426,
      "width": 633,
      "height": 202,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "#141517",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 470855,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 695648,
      "isDeleted": false
    },
    {
      "id": "diagram-mu42d03x-12_code",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 572,
      "y": 438,
      "width": 609,
      "height": 178,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 792080,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 842159,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "+----------------+      1. Place 16-bit Address      +----------------------+\n|                |==================================>|                      |\n|                |                                   |  Memory / I/O Port   |\n|                |      2. Assert RD' = 0 (Pulse)    |      Selection       |\n|  Intel 8085    |---------------------------------->|   (Address Decoder)  |\n| Microprocessor |                                   |                      |\n|                |      3. Drive Data on Data Bus    |                      |\n|                |<==================================|                      |\n|                |              (D7 - D0)            +----------------------+\n+----------------+",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
