        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-56_text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 4202,
      "width": 272,
      "height": 20,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 111563,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 785447,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Latched Persistent Data Output",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow-mu42d03x-56"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-52-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -676,
      "y": 4187,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 171,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 671296,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 460825,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Output peripherals require\ntransparent D-latches (IC 74LS373).\nBecause CPU bus data persists for\nonly ~300 ns, the latch captures\ndata on the falling edge of WR'\ncombined with device selection,\nholding output voltage levels\nindefinitely to drive external\ndisplays and actuators.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-54-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -362,
      "y": 4279,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 114,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 493208,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 822781,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "During an I/O Read cycle, address\ndecoder output gates with RD' to pulse\nthe tri-state buffer OE' low, bridging\nperipheral lines to the CPU data bus for\nthe precise duration of the T3 sampling\nphase.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42d03x-56-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 52,
      "y": 4279,
      "width": 298,
      "height": 95,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 245483,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 26580,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "During an I/O Write cycle, the address\ndecoder gates with WR' to pulse the\nlatch clock pin, capturing transient\ndata from D7-D0 and sustaining static\noutput drive indefinitely.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "diagram-mu42d03x-58",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 4167,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 286,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "#141517",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 636252,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 327786,
      "isDeleted": false
    },
    {
      "id": "diagram-mu42d03x-58_code",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 572,
      "y": 4179,
      "width": 656,
      "height": 262,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_4"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 534086,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 998088,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "   INPUT PORT (Tri-State Buffer - 74LS244)          OUTPUT PORT (Latch - 74LS373)\n   \n        Peripheral Input Data                         CPU Data Bus (D7 - D0)\n                 |                                               |\n                 v                                               v\n        +-----------------+                             +-----------------+\n        |  Tri-State Gate |                             |    D-Latch      |\n        +-----------------+                             +-----------------+\n                 |                                               |\n    Enable Pulse | (Active LOW)                     Clock Pulse  | (Falling Edge)\n    from Address +----------------+                 from Address +----------------+\n    Decoder & RD'                 |                 Decoder & WR'                 |\n                 v                |                              v                |\n         CPU Data Bus (D7-D0)     |                      Peripheral Output Pins   |\n    (Enabled ONLY during Read)    |                 (Holds data continuously)     |",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic-mu42d03x-61",
