      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_5"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 684243,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 678896,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Master 8-Point Engineering Comparison Matrix",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "sub-mu42d03x-71"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-62-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1173,
      "y": 4797,
      "width": 306,
      "height": 171,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_5"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 988400,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 567771,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "In Memory-Mapped I/O, peripherals are\ntreated as memory registers. The system\nassigns a full 16-bit address (A15-A0)\nwithin the 64 KB memory map directly to\neach I/O port. The CPU asserts memory\ncontrol signals: IO/M'=0, MEMR', and\nMEMW'. Accessible by all memory\ninstructions (MOV r, M; LDA; STA; ADD\nM).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-71-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1215,
      "y": 5013,
      "width": 306,
      "height": 246,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42d041_5"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 489932,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 73295,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "GTU Summer 2024 / 2025 (7 Marks): 1.\nAddress Bus: 16-bit (A15-A0) vs 8-bit\n(A7-A0); 2. Capacity: 64 KB shared vs\n256 isolated; 3. Control: IO/M'=0\n(MEMR/MEMW) vs IO/M'=1 (IOR/IOW); 4.\nInstructions: All memory ops (MOV, LDA,\nSTA, ADD M) vs IN/OUT only; 5. Target:\nAny register (A-L) vs Accumulator only;\n6. Arithmetic: Direct ALU execution on\nports vs Accumulator copy required; 7.\nDecoders: 16-bit complex vs 8-bit\nsimple; 8. Speed: 13 T-states vs 10\nT-states.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42d03x-64",
